> [1] BUT, this would have a problem... monsters/objects with the same 
> character. E.g. both door and spellbook can be '+'. The question would be  
> "how to determine what is what?"

You can get quite far, in fact. Through nethackoptions you can configure
different chars to be written depending on what it is. The reason I
don't use the full 256 range of characters is that xterm will only
display 191 of them, the rest are considered control characters. Now, 
some characters (e.g. escape, '^[') ARE control characters that nethack
uses to move the cursor around and change colors, but the rest will just
be output "as is". I suppose you would be able to use about 250
characters to distinguish dungeon features. If you can catch the colors
as well, you can multiply the number of different objects that you can
distinguish quite a lot. You can even use the same character position
for totally different things, provided that they are not drawn in the
same color.

